Not the whole search space, but about 80% of the "basis vectors," the
core concepts. I described this in an earlier posting, about a year
ago.

> As my list showed, at least the technological side of things is 
> greatly accelerating.  My points about the difficulty of determining 

And I agree that technology is accelerating. I haven't disputed this.
The issue is _science_, not gadgets and cataloguing of things.

> Nor, indeed, have you refuted any of my speculative suggestions
