> temporal communication, wormholes, etc. are all areas of active
> interest by top-flight physicists like Kip Thorne). Now, I happen

Refuting speculative suggestions is not what I set out to do, and I
don't seen this as having much to do with the issue of whether GP can
or will change dramatically the way science is done. Using GP to do
crossovers of different fields (as an example) may lead to new
"theories," but these theories will need to be tested and examined.
These speculative suggestions about time travel, quantum
teleportation, etc., are not likely to be tested anytime soon, so how
will GP help?
...
> its possibilities.  Of course, it would help if more physicists
